 "title": "Differentiating sums and multiples",
 "audience": "learner",
 "keyIdea": "Differentiate term by term. A number multiplying a term stays; a number on its own disappears.",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "You can differentiate a sum one term at a time. For y = x³ + x², dy/dx = 3x² + 2x.",
   "A number in front stays in front, so 5x² becomes 5 × 2x = 10x. A number on its own, like + 4, becomes 0. So y = 5x² + 3x + 4 gives dy/dx = 10x + 3."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "In symbols, the derivative of af + bg is af′ + bg′. This is what lets you differentiate any polynomial quickly.",
   "Products are different. The derivative of x²(x + 1) is not 2x × 1. Expand it first to x³ + x², then differentiate to get 3x² + 2x."
  ]
 },
